        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "2. Experiment",
          "quote": "The ingots were made by arc melting using commercially pure materials. A Nb addition alloy was also made with composition of Ti47 eTi45eNb8 (all the compositions in this work will be expressed in atomic percent) to make comparison with TiAl eRu. The materials were ﬂipped over and re-melted ﬁve times to ensure complete mixing. Pre-puriﬁed argon gas ﬂowed constantly through the furnace chamber during melting to prevent oxidation. Pure Ti buttons were used as a getter to further remove oxygen.",
